.TH SETREUID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setreuid \- sets the real and effective user ids; (uid_t)-1 leaves an id unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int setreuid(uid_t real, uid_t effective);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the real and effective user IDs; (uid_t)-1 leaves an ID unchanged. This is a direct per-thread syscall.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setreuid (2)
